[00:23.94] Saint Stephen with a rose, in and out of the garden he goes,
[00:29.18] Country garden in the wind and the rain,
[00:31.74] Wherever he goes the people all complain.
[00:34.84] Stephen prospered in his time, well he may and he may decline.
[00:40.12] Did it matter, does it now? Stephen would answer if he only knew how.
[00:59.24] Wishing well with a golden bell, bucket hanging clear to hell,
[01:04.48] Hell halfway twixt now and then,
[01:07.22] Stephen fill it up and lower down and lower down again.
[01:20.94] Lady finger, dipped in moonlight,
[01:26.96] Writing "What for?" across the morning sky.
[01:34.68] Sunlight splatters, dawn with answer,
[01:42.12] Darkness shrugs and bids the day goodbye.
[01:48.94] Speeding arrow, sharp and narrow,
[01:54.90] What a lot of fleeting matters you have spurned.
[02:03.32] Several seasons with their treasons,
[02:10.36] Wrap the babe in scarlet colors, call it your own.
[02:27.18] Did he doubt or did he try? Answers aplenty in the bye and bye,
[02:32.18] Talk about your plenty, talk about your ills,
[02:34.94] One man gathers what another man spills.
[03:05.70] Saint Stephen will remain, all he's lost he shall regain,
[03:10.88] Seashore washed by the suds and foam,
[03:13.32] Been here so long, he's got to calling it home.
[03:16.46] Fortune comes a crawlin', calliope woman,
[03:21.72] Spinnin' that curious sense of your own.
[03:27.48] Can you answer? Yes I can.
[03:32.26] But what would be the answer to the answer man?
